1. **A wearable garment system**, comprising:  

   a garment configured to be worn on a body of a user, the garment including a plurality of sensor attachment locations distributed at different anatomical regions of the garment;  

   a plurality of wireless biometric sensor modules, each wireless biometric sensor module being removably attachable to any one of the plurality of sensor attachment locations and comprising:  
   (i) at least one biometric sensor configured to generate biometric sensor data;  
   (ii) a position-identification circuit configured to determine, upon attachment of the wireless biometric sensor module to one of the plurality of sensor attachment locations, location information identifying the sensor attachment location to which the wireless biometric sensor module is attached;  
   (iii) a processor configured to select, based at least in part on the location information, one or more signal types from a plurality of available signal types for transmission; and  
   (iv) a wireless communication circuit configured to wirelessly transmit data corresponding to the selected one or more signal types; and  

   a receiver device configured to receive the wirelessly transmitted data from the plurality of wireless biometric sensor modules,  

   wherein each wireless biometric sensor module automatically configures its transmitted biometric data according to the identified sensor attachment location such that different ones of the plurality of wireless biometric sensor modules transmit different selected signal types when attached to different anatomical regions of the garment.

1. A wearable biometric sensing system comprising:  

   a controller; and  

   a plurality of wireless biometric sensors configured to be selectively attached to different locations on an article of clothing, each wireless biometric sensor comprising:  

   a sensor-location reader configured to read a location identifier associated with a respective attachment location on the article of clothing;  

   an electrode interface configured to electrically couple the wireless biometric sensor to one or more electrodes positioned at or proximate the respective attachment location;  

   biometric sensing circuitry configured to acquire biometric signals from the one or more electrodes;  

   a wireless communication circuit configured to communicate with the controller; and  

   processing circuitry configured to determine, based at least in part on the location identifier, biometric data relevant to the respective attachment location and to cause the wireless communication circuit to transmit to the controller only the biometric data determined to be relevant to the respective attachment location.

2. The wearable biometric sensing system of claim 1, wherein the location identifier comprises at least one of an RFID tag, an NFC tag, a barcode, a QR code, a magnetic code, an electrical resistance value, or a conductive pattern.

3. The wearable biometric sensing system of claim 1, wherein the processing circuitry is configured to select one or more signal processing parameters based on the location identifier.

4. The wearable biometric sensing system of claim 1, wherein the processing circuitry is configured to suppress, discard, or refrain from transmitting biometric signals that are not associated with the respective attachment location.

5. The wearable biometric sensing system of claim 1, wherein the one or more electrodes are integrated into the article of clothing.

6. The wearable biometric sensing system of claim 1, wherein the biometric data comprises at least one of electrocardiogram data, electromyogram data, respiration data, impedance data, heart-rate data, or motion-correlated biometric data.

7. The wearable biometric sensing system of claim 1, wherein each wireless biometric sensor is removably attachable to any of a plurality of attachment locations on the article of clothing and is configured to automatically configure itself based on the location identifier read at the attachment location.

8. The wearable biometric sensing system of claim 1, wherein the controller is configured to receive biometric data from the plurality of wireless biometric sensors and associate the received biometric data with body locations corresponding to the respective location identifiers.

9. A method for operating a wearable biometric sensing system, the method comprising:  

   attaching a wireless biometric sensor to an attachment location on an article of clothing;  

   reading, by the wireless biometric sensor, a location identifier associated with the attachment location;  

   electrically coupling the wireless biometric sensor to one or more electrodes associated with the attachment location;  

   acquiring biometric signals from the one or more electrodes;  

   determining, based at least in part on the location identifier, which biometric data is relevant to the attachment location; and  

   wirelessly transmitting, from the wireless biometric sensor to a controller, only the biometric data determined to be relevant to the attachment location.

10. The method of claim 9, further comprising configuring at least one of a sensing mode, sampling rate, filtering parameter, gain setting, or data-reporting format based on the location identifier.

11. The method of claim 9, further comprising preventing transmission of biometric data not corresponding to a body region associated with the location identifier.

12. A wireless biometric sensor for use with an article of clothing having a plurality of sensor attachment locations, the wireless biometric sensor comprising:  

   an attachment structure configured to removably attach the wireless biometric sensor to any one of the plurality of sensor attachment locations;  

   a location-identification circuit configured to read a location identifier at an attached one of the plurality of sensor attachment locations;  

   an electrode connector configured to connect to one or more clothing-supported electrodes;  

   biometric acquisition circuitry configured to acquire biometric signals through the electrode connector;  

   a wireless transmitter configured to transmit data to a controller; and  

   a processor configured to identify a body location corresponding to the location identifier and to control the wireless transmitter to transmit biometric data selected according to the identified body location.
